<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n4919" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">baptisma</span></b> , ătis,
		n., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βάπτισμα</span>. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A dipping in</i>, <i>dipping
			under</i>, <i>washing</i>, <i>ablution</i>, <i><span class="en">Prud. Psych. 103</span></i>;
			Apoth. 697; <i><span class="en">Vulg. Marc. 7, 4</span></i>; <i><span class="en">7, 8</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">mundi,</span>”
				i. e. <i>the general deluge</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Tert. Bapt. 8</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			Esp., <i>Christian baptism</i>, <i><span class="en">Vulg. Eph. 4,
				5</span></i>; in the Church fathers very freq.—A parallel
			form <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">baptismus</span></b> ,
			i, m., Cod. Th. 16, 6, 1; <i><span class="en">Vulg.
				Marc. 11, 30 al.</span></i>—<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">baptismum</span></b> , i, n.,
					<i><span class="en">Tert. Bapt. 15</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Aug. Serm. Temp. 36</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Vulg.
				Matt. 21, 25 al.</span></i></div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Latin Dictionary</u>
        </u> (Charlton T. Lewis, Charles Short, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1879) </div>
